{% set local_problem %}
<p>Toney properties are often surrounded by mature trees — oaks, pines, maples, and whatever else has been growing for decades. That natural beauty comes with a gutter problem: constant debris.</p>

<p>Pine needles fall year-round, not just in autumn. Oak leaves blanket everything in fall. And rural properties don't have the luxury of municipal cleanup — that debris sits on your roof and in your gutters until you deal with it.</p>

<p>Without gutter guards, you're looking at cleaning gutters 4-6 times per year on heavily wooded lots. That's a lot of ladder time on rural properties where single-story homes aren't always the norm.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters. They allow water in while blocking leaves, pine needles, and debris. The right system for your property depends on what type of debris you're dealing with.</p>

<p>For Toney's heavily wooded lots, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. Unlike basic screens that let fine debris through, micro-mesh blocks everything — including those problematic pine needles. Water flows through; debris stays out.</p>

<p>We'll assess your specific situation during a free estimate and recommend the best solution for your tree coverage and gutter configuration.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed gutter guards on rural properties throughout northwest Madison County for over 20 years. We know that Toney's tree coverage is different from suburban Madison, and we select products accordingly.</p>

<p>Our team will assess your property honestly. If your current gutters need work before guards make sense, we'll tell you. If a less expensive option will work for your situation, we'll recommend it. That's how neighbors treat neighbors.</p>
